From d8ce1d2e76f6c8c1e976ab3dc4f21d65b9f9aec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thom Hadfield <100659456+festeraeb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:06:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] mesh port: a request cancelled by stop() is never re-sent

During stop(), cancel_all() aborts a pipe still waiting on its device.
proxy_request then reported it as unanswered (502), so the auto router
re-sent it to the next device after the pipe list was cleared: that
request escaped cancellation, could run inference during shutdown, and
could hold the listener join for its 300 s read timeout.

- proxy_request reports a three-way ProxyOutcome: Answered, Unanswered,
  or Cancelled. The auto router re-sends only Unanswered.
- cancel_all() closes the proxy set under its lock, and add() refuses a
  pipe once it is closed, so every pipe is either cancelled by
  cancel_all() or never started. bind_listener() reopens it (start and
  the TLS switch).
- forward_to_node returns Cancelled at once when the set is closed.

New test StopDoesNotReSendACancelledAutoRequest fails without this
change (the fallback device received the request, auto_failovers 1).
ctest -R "Sdk|Mesh": 411/411 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
